This is an additional argument for <s>Brahman</s>'s material causality.
<s>Brahman</s> is the material cause for this further reason, that <s>Brahman</s> itself is directly stated as the cause, taking up both origination and dissolution: 'All these beings arise from space (<s>ākāśa</s>) alone;
they return into space' (<s>Chāndogya</s> 1.9.1).

Even there, for the <s>jīva</s> enveloped by waters, [the leech-analogy] is compared merely to the extension of the mental conception directed toward the body-to-be-attained, which is presented by <s>karma</s> — there is no contradiction.
Thus, when the manner of attaining another body has been stated by <s>śruti</s>, all speculations arising from human intellect — such as [the view that] the all-pervading instruments and the self acquire their function in the [new] body-to-be-attained through the <s>karma</s>-trace;
or [the view that] the self alone acquires its function there;
